From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:25:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] wasm: optimize static execution and native value
 boundaries

Expose a native UTF-8 string writer to Static Hermes extern calls and
allow Hermes string values as native arguments. Snapshot own enumerable
entries without JavaScript pair-array allocation, preserving getter and
proxy order.

Construct decoded objects using bounded runtime-local shape templates and
dense arrays through native slots. Keep templates rooted and independent
of document values; use general own-property definitions for indexed or
duplicate keys and mutable dictionary shapes. Add native descriptor
snapshots that compare data, accessors, symbols, prototypes and flags
without constructing descriptor objects or invoking accessors.

Emit compiled regex literal bytecode in Static Hermes C output while
creating fresh RegExp objects and retaining named-group initialization.
Add selective static recognition of original Math methods, excluding
random, and lower numeric imul to unsigned modulo-32-bit multiplication.
Other operands retain JavaScript coercion through the builtin call.

Validate object isolation and GC roots, descriptor mutations and SameValue
semantics, regex identity and state, numeric conversions, preserved host
replacements, and emitted native helper calls.

Resolve native object layouts from borrowed key bytes, compare collisions by
key content, and evict individual least-recently-used layouts. Build immutable
classes directly and decode values through callbacks into initialized, rooted
object and array storage. Retain explicit fallbacks for wide, indexed and
duplicate-key objects and expose construction counters without allocation.

Return the original primitive for full-range string slices and scan unchanged
ASCII case conversions before allocating temporary UTF-16 storage. Cache string
prototype data-property slots in Static Hermes while preserving replacements,
accessor receivers and prototype mutations.

Cache computed own data-property reads by weak shape and interned key, with
bounded per-site storage and generic semantics for unsupported objects and
keys. Trace both weak class and symbol references, and initialize private-name
cache counts in every generated unit.

Inline guarded numeric typed-array reads and proven-number bit operations.
Preserve attachment and bounds checks, numeric coercion, NaN boxing, and generic
fallbacks for unsupported element kinds and keys. Include mirrored runtime
layouts in the Static Hermes ABI descriptor.

Expose numeric heap and cumulative GC statistics for opt-in execution
observation without JavaScript allocation or heap traversal. Validate normal
and small-C computed loads, GC invalidation, detached arrays, numeric edges,
and the native value adapter against host and Wasm builds.

Retain two receiver shapes at ordinary named-read sites and two shape/key
pairs per computed-cache set without enlarging the computed cache. Keep
weak roots, prototype validation, accessors and dictionary-mode fallbacks.
Add direct present-storage reads for ordinary arrays while retaining
inherited lookup for holes and unsupported keys.

Propagate known closure code through bounded parameter, phi and return
analysis while preserving the actual closure environment. Permit bounded
Static Hermes inlining of small field readers into try/catch callers when
a fresh object argument exposes allocation and field operations to existing
object promotion. Keep other backends' inlining policy unchanged.

Lower proven numeric abs, ceil, floor, trunc, round and binary min/max with
shared JavaScript rounding, NaN and signed-zero semantics. Fuse eligible
numeric string-index comparisons with one UTF-16 code unit; guard unknown
receivers and preserve prototype lookup, GC roots and exception cleanup.

Validate callback identity and environments, inlining growth, object
elimination, cache invalidation, indexed reads and numeric/string edges in
host and Wasm execution, including normal and small-C output. Retain the
existing native value-adapter and runtime ABI checks.

Prove bounded signed/unsigned integer ranges through producers and phi inputs,
remove idempotent conversions, and consume those proofs in numeric bitwise and
imul emission. Keep general conversions for unknown values and preserve BigInt
coercion through objects. The existing numeric type factories remain unchanged.

Share one indexed character read across strict single-code-unit comparisons.
Preserve the property read position, key coercion, inherited values and errors;
root receiver and key through fallback getters and collection.

Index Unicode and legacy case transforms with immutable page directories.
Retain crossing ranges and compare every supported code point against the
original transform mapping, including surrogates and out-of-domain values.

Call known always-callable closure targets through their native entry while
retaining the actual closure environment. Distribute copies of unaliased
branch-local object literals into their incoming ordinary branch edges so
existing promotion removes the temporary allocations. Preserve field order,
source evaluation and exception regions; retain general spread semantics for
observable sources and unknown layouts.

Validate integer boundaries and coercions, shared character reads, native-call
environments, conditional spreads and iterator cleanup in optimized/unoptimized
native, bytecode, and normal/small-C Wasm execution. Existing optimizer, Unicode
and split-C linking regressions pass. Inspect linked Wasm and native code for
removed conversion and generic character-read work without claiming runtime
speedup from static counts.

Retain bounded Static Hermes C allocation layouts across source edits. Keep
string indices, native function slots, property-cache ranges, dense captured
variables and shard membership stable where current shapes still match.
Prefer unique environment consumers over occurrence-matched duplicate getters;
limit duplicate closure context to property publication and small creators.

Seed serialized literal pools by exact byte segments and retain separate shape
slots for ordinary, typed and non-enumerable typed allocations. Preserve current
serialization, overlapping storage and direct runtime access. Skip empty storage
appends so unchanged literal pools do not acquire alignment padding.

Emit an authenticated layout descriptor separately from C translation units.
Validate and bound every retained table, and discard excessive retired hints for
the next compilation without regenerating already lowered IR. Layouts remain
optional, all current code regenerates, and native object reuse still requires
exact emitted bytes. Validate edited sources, restored inputs, malformed seeds,
compaction, typed shapes, closure environments and split-C native execution in
114 compiler cases and 36 native executions.

Retain bounded field/effect analysis, private helper argument promotion,
guarded data-property definitions and byte-array loop lowering. Keep record
return forwarding and late materialization outside the default pipeline where
their dynamic benefit is not established. Extend normalization reuse to fresh
flat string arrays with invocation-owned guards, independent result copies,
bounded misses and actual backing-storage retention charges.

Use a GC-traced native Promise core behind explicit runtime activation and
drive compiler-generated async state machines without continuation closures.
Preserve reactions, thenable assimilation, rejection and cleanup ordering,
reentrant collection, tracing configuration and bytecode/compiled callers.
Expose only the existing public Promise surface after bootstrap.

Borrow already-rooted values across native construction boundaries, reuse
eligible UTF-8 conversions within an invocation, and split exception helpers
into separately optimized generated C. Preserve source evaluation, coercion,
GC roots, exception cleanup and deterministic layout identities.

Validate semantic edges with optimizer, native and Wasm fixtures, including
closure environments, malformed layout hints, Promise/async conformance,
collection during callbacks and bounded string-storage retention. Retain
explicit activation and unsupported-path semantics for experimental passes.

Aggregate guarded dense arrays of native Promises and primitives using shared
traced state and native reactions. Avoid temporary capabilities, per-element
closures and descriptors, and discarded chained Promises while preserving
settlement order, rejection tracking and observable method overrides. Keep
unsupported inputs on the existing JavaScript implementation and bound array
admission to 4096 elements.

Keep aggregation entries separate from ordinary Promise dispatch. Return private
bootstrap hooks positionally and capture the aggregation function directly,
avoiding extra interned method names and repeated method lookup. Retain the
existing primitive-resolution behavior, array exposure and freezing semantics,
and GC safety during queued callbacks and reentrant collection.

Validate native and compiled callers with override, adoption, rejection,
signed-zero, bounds, array-exposure and GC cases.

Prepare compiler-described ordinary literal layouts before initialized-image
capture. Root each unit's prepared classes in long-lived GC-managed storage,
populate descendant maps before parent maps, and preserve prepared parent
lookup storage when constructing descendants. Ordinary, typed and private
layouts retain distinct eligibility and existing allocation semantics.

Expose runtime-owned preparation and young-reclamation boundaries. Perform
full collection for preparation, return only verified empty nursery payload,
and defer young-only maintenance when old-generation progress is required.
Keep survivor tracing, finalizers and ordinary GC authority intact.

Validate prepared parent/child maps across units and collection, deferred young
reclamation, 115 compiler layout cases and 37 native executions. Build both
host and Wasm runtime archives without claiming complete embedding acceptance.
